<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bodhachandra Singh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1908–1955</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bodhachandra Singh was the last ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> of Manipur, succeeding his father Churachand Singh in 1941. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-independence">Indian independence</a> Manipur adopted its own constitution and held elections in 1948, but in September 1949 he signed a merger agreement in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shillong">Shillong</a>, and Manipur joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> that October as a centrally administered state. It became a full state in 1972.</p></div>
